# A driver writes its returns under `/output/`. That directory is ignored, and an ignored
# directory is exactly what permanently lost the laboratory's tiger phase-atlas figures and
# `semantics_invariant_under_exact_chart.lean` — only a name, a proof term and a SHA-256 survive,
# at no commit in either repository.
#
# So what carries standing does not stay here. It is DEPOSITED into `/standing/`, which is tracked,
# bound to its content hash AND to the closure hash of the founding that produced it. See
# `standing/README.md` and `soma/tools/standing-deposit/`. A return that is only ever written to
# `/output/` is a return the repository cannot certify and can lose.
/target/
/output/
/runs/
/data/
/tmp/
*.log

# Lake writes every generated artifact under a project's `.lake/` directory: compiled `.olean`
# and `.ilean` output, the C intermediate, and the third-party package cache (Mathlib alone is
# 9.2-9.6 GiB, see archive/cpp-engine/provenance/LABORATORY_ONLY.md). None of it is source and
# none of it is tracked.
#
# Lean PROJECT SOURCES are not under `.lake/` and are not ignored: `soma/formal/*/lakefile.toml`,
# `soma/formal/*/lean-toolchain`, `soma/formal/*/lake-manifest.json`, and every `.lean` file
# beside them are tracked. Kernel scratch written by a driver belongs under `/output/`, which is
# ignored above; it must not be written under `.lake/`, where a tracked file would match this
# pattern and the repository's only formal artifacts would be generated fixtures.
**/.lake/

# Python bytecode from `tools/`. The tools are sources; their caches are not.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# A driver return that landed at the root before its default path was corrected (2026-08-08).
# Returns belong under `/output/`, where the manifest can certify them.
/holonic-eta-ratio-atlas.ron

# Third-party transcripts held for reference. `reference/**` asserts nothing (THE_DOCUMENT_LAW §1),
# and these are not this project's material to redistribute: they are working sources, cited in short
# attributed fragments by the records that use them and never carried in the tree.
reference/external/3b1b-compression-*

# Agent worktrees. The harness mounts a full checkout per isolated agent under `.claude/worktrees/`,
# each with its own `target/`. Measured 2026-08-13: four abandoned worktrees from 08-10 and 08-11
# holding 223 GB inside the repository, untracked and NOT ignored — one `git add -A` from being
# staged. They are scratch: what an agent returns is its report, and any edit it made belongs in
# the main tree or nowhere. Remove them with `git worktree remove`, never by deleting the directory.
.claude/
